---
import Profile from '../layouts/Profile.astro';
import WorkstationMedia from '../components/WorkstationMedia.astro';
import SelectedProducts from '../components/SelectedProducts.astro';
import '../styles/workstation.css';
---
<Profile page="home" footerMessage={{title: 'Get in touch', body: 'I’m interested in design engineering and product-building roles, especially interfaces for AI tools and complex workflows. Based in Des Moines; open to relocation.'}}>
  <section class="hero wrap">
    <div>
      <h1>I design and build products for complex workflows.</h1>
      <p class="lede">My work includes study tools, vehicle comparison, and tools for AI agents. I use AI coding tools from product direction through interface design, implementation, and iteration.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button" href="#selected-work">View selected work</a>
        <a href="/dave-bettner-resume.pdf" download>Download résumé</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="scene-wrap"><WorkstationMedia /></div>
  </section>
  <section id="selected-work" class="section selected-work wrap">
    <h2>Selected work</h2>
    <SelectedProducts />
  </section>
  <section id="building" class="section implementation wrap">
    <h2>From a user problem to working software.</h2>
    <p>I own product direction, interface design, and implementation for Passal and Leasekite, working through AI coding tools. I use those tools to explore alternatives, build the experience, and work through changes. My customer-delivery background shapes the workflow questions I start with.</p>
    <div class="case-links"><a href="/fit/#building">How I build</a><a href="/work/">Products and agent tools</a></div>
  </section>
  <section class="section background-tools wrap">
    <div class="experience">
      <h2>Customer delivery background</h2>
      <p>At Citrin Cooperman, I managed a five-person implementation team. At Workiva, I led 6–12 concurrent implementations. Today, I’m a Senior Manager at LSL, leading Workiva delivery for city and county finance teams.</p>
      <p>At LSL, I scope consulting engagements, prepare estimates and statements of work, and lead Workiva delivery for city and county finance teams through client sign-off. I also build Python reporting tools reused across engagements, with human review before client changes.</p>
      <div class="case-links"><a href="/experience/">Career history</a><a href="/experience/connected-reporting/">Connected-reporting implementation</a><a href="/fit/#scope">Scope and client enablement</a></div>
    </div>
    <div class="technical-work">
      <h2>Technical tools</h2>
      <div class="projects">
        <article class="project">
          <div>
            <h3><a href="/work/accounting-acceptance-lab/">Accounting Acceptance Lab</a></h3>
            <p>Testing whether accounting agents use the right evidence and recover without duplicate ledger changes. Synthetic accounting cases.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <a href="/work/accounting-acceptance-lab/" aria-label="About the project: Accounting Acceptance Lab">Details</a>
            <a href="https://github.com/dbett4/accounting-acceptance-lab" aria-label="View repository: Accounting Acceptance Lab">View repository</a>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="project">
          <div>
            <h3><a href="/work/regulated-reporting-mcp/">Regulated Reporting MCP</a></h3>
            <p>Exploring limits on AI agents changing reports, with caller-confirmed default writes. Mock-data demo.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <a href="/work/regulated-reporting-mcp/" aria-label="About the project: Regulated Reporting MCP">Details</a>
            <a href="https://github.com/dbett4/regulated-reporting-mcp" aria-label="View repository: Regulated Reporting MCP">View repository</a>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
      <a class="section-link" href="/work/">More technical work</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Profile>
